  "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
  "instance_name": "mapping_001",
  "label": "The man is mapped as 'my brother' delivering moral advice",
  "description": "The top text 'my brother, the more girlfriends you have...' explicitly identifies the visual entity (the Black man) as 'my brother'. This creates an analogical mapping where the man is being projected as a moral authority figure ('my brother') who is giving advice. The visual material (the man's serious expression) is mapped onto the textual role of 'my brother' who is delivering a warning. This mapping reinforces the stereotype that Black men are inherently moral authorities or figures of wisdom, which is part of the racialized moralistic trope.",
